{
  "about": "Reference vectors for PROTOCOL.md \"File transfer\". All byte values are hex. \"payload\" is the message payload and \"frame\" the whole inner message ([type][4-byte length][payload]) before SECURE wraps it. JSON payloads have no fixed byte form, so the offer entries are checks of the reading, not of bytes: \"valid\" says whether a receiver may accept the offer and \"offer\" what it reads from it; an offer that is not valid is declined with status 1 when \"answerable\" (its id is then given) and ignored otherwise. \"names\" gives the file name a receiver stores for an offered name, and \"freeNames\" the name used when some are taken (\"taken\" stands for what the file system reports; these cases compare exactly). \"sequences\" follow one accepted incoming transfer: each step is a message from the sender, \"reply\" what the receiver sends back (absent: nothing) and \"state\" where the transfer stands afterwards.",
  "version": 1,
  "messageTypes": {
    "FILE_OFFER": 88,
    "FILE_ANSWER": 89,
    "FILE_DATA": 90,
    "FILE_END": 91
  },
